03:48.910 --> 03:52.470
All right friends, now we come to a very interesting use case for the isnull.

03:52.630 --> 04:00.110
And that is by introducing a new type of joins between tables that's going to help us to find the unmatching

04:00.110 --> 04:01.990
rows between two tables.

04:02.030 --> 04:06.670
Let's have a quick recap about the joins in SQL in order to understand the new types.

04:06.670 --> 04:09.510
So basically we have two sets or let's say two tables.

04:09.710 --> 04:11.270
The left and the right.

04:11.310 --> 04:16.950
And if you go and use an inner join what we are doing here, we are finding only the matching rows between

04:16.950 --> 04:19.030
the left table and the right table.

04:19.030 --> 04:22.030
So at the result we will get only the matching rows.

04:22.070 --> 04:25.990
Now we have another type of joins called left outer join.

04:25.990 --> 04:27.310
And if you use this type.

04:27.350 --> 04:27.990
Add the result.

04:27.990 --> 04:32.510
You will get all the rows from the left table and as well only the.

04:32.550 --> 04:34.870
Matching rows from the right table.

04:34.910 --> 04:37.630
Now we have another type which is exactly the opposite.

04:37.830 --> 04:38.990
The right join.

04:38.990 --> 04:42.750
And here we are going to get all the rows from the right table and only.

04:42.790 --> 04:45.750
The matching informations from the left table.

04:45.790 --> 04:47.590
And now to the last type that we learned.

04:47.630 --> 04:48.710
We have the full join.

04:48.710 --> 04:53.190
We will get all the rows from the left and as well all the rows from the right.

04:53.230 --> 04:55.190
So we will not be missing anything.

04:55.190 --> 04:58.630
So those are the four basic joins that we have learned in SQL.

04:58.670 --> 05:02.750
But in SQL we have as well other types that are more advanced.

05:02.750 --> 05:05.550
But we don't have in SQL any keywords for that.

05:05.670 --> 05:09.190
So the first one called left Antijoin.

05:09.190 --> 05:16.270
So what we are saying here, we need all the rows from the left table, but this time without the matching

05:16.270 --> 05:16.830
rows.

05:16.830 --> 05:22.350
So all the informations that are matching with the right table, we don't want to see it at the results.

05:22.350 --> 05:26.500
And as I said, we don't have here an extra keyword for this type of join.

05:26.500 --> 05:31.780
But in order to get this effect, we're going to go and combine the left join together with the Isnull.

05:31.780 --> 05:36.780
And with that, we're going to get all the data from the left side, but without anything that is matching

05:36.780 --> 05:37.660
the right side.

05:37.660 --> 05:39.820
And this we call it left Anti-join.

05:39.820 --> 05:44.700
And we have another advanced type for the joins called the right anti-join.

05:44.700 --> 05:46.100
This is exactly the opposite.

05:46.100 --> 05:53.420
So we are saying all the rows from the right table without having any matching rows from the left table.

05:53.420 --> 05:57.100
So all the information on the right side that is not matching the left side.

05:57.100 --> 05:59.380
So again here we don't have a keyword for that.

05:59.380 --> 06:03.180
We're going to go and work with the right join plus and Isnull.

06:03.180 --> 06:08.140
So with that as you can see we have two new types of joins added to our four basic joins.

06:08.180 --> 06:09.660
Now this might be confusing.

